{% extends 'site/base_public.html.twig' %}

{#
   Formations, on the shared catalogue shells — the seventh and last.

   ⚠️ A formation is the only thing in the app with a PROGRESSION, and that is
   exactly why the head/foot split holds rather than breaks: progress is a fact
   about YOU, so it belongs in the footer beside "libre-service" and "obtenu",
   not in the head beside "libre" and "occupée".

   ⚠️ Deliberately NO progress bar, decided with the operator. It would not have
   been different code — one more optional slot, like `state` or `tiles` — but
   it would have been used on two pages out of seven, and machines, espaces,
   matériaux, annuaires and badges have no proportion to show without inventing
   one. That is the component S51 wrote and deleted before commit because
   nothing referenced it. Text only; seven pages stay strictly identical.

   ⚠️ This is the LIST only. `formation-suivi` is 1 199 lines and belongs to
   S48; folding it in here would turn a catalogue session into an LMS refit.
#}

{% block title %}{{ 'nav.trainings'|trans }} - FabOS{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('css/machines-list.css') ~ '?v=' ~ css_version }}">
{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
{% embed 'site/_catalogue.html.twig' with {
    available_word: 'common.validated_short'|trans,
    route: 'app_formations',
    title: 'nav.trainings'|trans,
    tiles: tiles,
    tile_all_label: 'machines.all_short'|trans,
    show_tile_icons: false,
    filter_key: 'cat',
    filter_value: category,
    search: search,
    total: totalCount,
    all: allCount,
    unit: 'formation',
    unit_plural: 'formations',
    headline_count: signedIn ? doneCount : 0,
    headline_label: 'state.done_count'|trans,
    empty_text: 'formations.none_found'|trans,
} %}
    {% block cards %}
        {% for entry in cards %}
            {% set f = entry.formation %}
            {# ⚠️ Three tones, not two: finished is the thing a member is looking for
               in this list, and it read as grey — the same weight as "non commencée",
               which is its opposite. Green is safe on this card because /formations
               passes no head `state` chip, so there is no second green to collide
               with; see the note beside .ml-req-ok in machines-list.css before
               reusing `ok` elsewhere.
               ⚠️ The comment lives HERE and not inside the hash below: a Twig
               comment is not an expression, so placing one between two keys of an
               argument hash is a syntax error. It shipped that way once.
               ⚠️ And never write a comment-close sequence inside comment prose —
               Twig ends the comment at the FIRST one, and everything after it is
               emitted as page text. That shipped too: a sentence from this very
               note appeared on /formations, in a grid cell of its own. #}
            {# 🔴 `photo: f.image` produced `<img src="/laser">` on every card — eight
               broken-image placeholders. `Formation.image` does not hold a path: its
               values are `laser`, `printer-3d`, `cnc`, `soldering`… i.e. icon slugs,
               and `asset('laser')` resolves to `/laser`, which 404s. The column is
               misnamed, not the template.
               ⚠️ The slug passed is `f.categorie`, not `f.image`: `_category_icon`
               is documented as taking a CATEGORY slug and its mapping is keyed on
               French words, so "Découpe laser" and "Électronique" resolve correctly
               where "laser" and "soldering" would both fall through to the generic
               printer icon. #}
            {% include 'site/_catalogue_card.html.twig' with {
                url: path('app_formation_detail', {id: f.id}),
                title: f.titre,
                type: f.categorie,
                meta: f.badge ? 'state.unlocks_badge'|trans ~ ' ' ~ f.badge.nom : '',
                note: f.duree,
                icon_slug: f.categorie|default(''),
                foot: signedIn
                    ? (entry.completed ? 'state.done'|trans
                        : (entry.started ? 'state.doing'|trans : 'state.todo'|trans))
                    : '',
                foot_icon: signedIn and entry.completed ? 'check' : '',
                foot_tone: signedIn and entry.completed ? 'go'
                    : (signedIn and entry.started ? 'caution' : 'muted'),
                action: 'machines.see'|trans,
            } only %}
        {% endfor %}
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
{% endblock %}
